{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1410842-what-about-secret-conventions-that-most-of-the-other-technocrats-don-t-know-exist","id":1410842,"title":"What about Secret Conventions that most of the Other Technocrats don't know exist?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-08-28T07:09:39-07:00","id":1410842,"title":"<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/icons/icon3.png\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" alt=\"\" /> What about Secret Conventions that most of the Other Technocrats don't know exist?","content":"Just a thought how the NWO has a lot of control over thought and global psychology and well pretty much they seem to be the quintessential Technocrats. Control is a hyper secret and uber compromised Controlling Organ of the Technocracy. So what if there are secret facets of the Technocracy hidden from the vast majority of the Organization. What I am first thinking of is a sort of Time Cop Convention. Like I think back to Star Trek and the Department of Temporal Investigations who are in charge of keeping the Timeline clean, and others like Immortus and the Council of Kangs obsessed over control of the Timeline. An Adjudicators of Temporal Harmony Convention would be interesting, as it could explore the idea of the Technocracy managing a hidden front of the Ascension War normally only observed by Archmagi. They could have their handful with incidents similar to the Week of Nightmares and the normies among the Awakened would be none the wiser. It could also represent a weird notion that Control is aware of the wider Multiverse and have some level of communication with their counterparts in other Timelines/Universe.<br /> <br /> I can see Agents being recruited from the vetted newly awakened and essentially disappearing as they join the ranks of Time Barristers or Magistrates from the Past and Future. And if used as PCs then you could have justifiable cause to make characters with really out there backstories like folks from a collapsed Timeline that experienced the Time of Judgement or fell to Gehenna, or just an Enlightened Artisan who was just too revolutionary for the timetable and removed from Sorcerers Crusade Era.<br /> <br /> They could even be twin group with one assigned to Parallel Worlds while the Temporal group handles the actual timelines. I guess Correspondence would be a good one for the sister organization, even though Multiverse travel is kind of beyond normal levels of Correspondence, So maybe a Prime Convention to link the Three Conventions?<br /> <br /> What are your thoughts on the Idea of Secret Conventions? They could even be outside Control's well control and could be very carefully unknotting the mess that is the compromised Control.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-28T07:15:45-07:00","id":1410843,"title":"","content":"Imo your better off having more secret factions rather then full blown conventions. Project Invictus and The Friends of John Courage come to mind.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3953-dwight","name":"Dwight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3953_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2355"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-28T07:21:30-07:00","id":1410845,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dwight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1410842-what-about-secret-conventions-that-most-of-the-other-technocrats-don-t-know-exist?p=1410843#post1410843\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Imo your better off having more secret factions rather then full blown conventions. Project Invictus and The Friends of John Courage come to mind.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah it actually started with me thinking of them as such, but then I went off the reservation and into full blown Homebrew Thought experiment territory with the idea of what if the Technocracy actually does have 9 Conventions! :P","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-28T08:45:19-07:00","id":1410853,"title":"","content":"Maybe one dealing with quantum mechanics?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23952-konradleijon","name":"Konradleijon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23952_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1441"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-30T09:47:53-07:00","id":1411084,"title":"","content":"A few years ago the Mage players became aware of a secret Convention called Section VII and, ultimately, its nefarious purpose. The Convention was very interested the power of belief and myth-making. Magic shouldn't happen, but it does. There were dragons, but the Consensus drove them away. Enlightened operatives and, if Ivory Tower records are any guide, Tradition mages seem guided by personified forms of inspiration that are known to reappear over successive generations. Some of these &quot;avatars&quot; (to use the Reality Deviant term) inspire their human associates to become really, really powerful (or at least very annoying and resistant to easy removal). <br /> <br /> But maybe those avatars could go the way of dragons? Not exactly, but Section VII found that by influencing media, folklore, urban legend, and commercialization, they could inhibit the return of some avatars. It's hard to be inspired by a being that is completely different than your conceptualization of it. One of their greatest successes was with the Akashic Brother who called himself Po Banyan, whose shining blue ki-rin avatar, Bae, would physically manifest for Sleepers to see when the mage drew upon his strange abilities. His staff could knock down trees, though he put more effort into knocking out the loggers harvesting them. <br /> <br /> Likewise, John Chapman, a mage following his own calling, produced cider that enhanced one's appreciation of the world around them, of togetherness and being at ease. He planted his apples across the country, and even (inadvertently) influenced presidential candidate William H Harrison into adopting the log cabin and hard cider as campaign themes. This was strongly at odds with the Technocratic view of human industry. The Progenitors quickly took care of President Harrison; Section VII dealt with Mr Chapman a few years later. This wasn't as successful, as his legend is deeply ingrained in the American psyche, but by manipulating what was known, they've manipulated what can be. They worked with Henrietta Lacks, too, but in a manner too convoluted to go into. <br /> <br /> Because this line of inquiry required acceptance of so much esoteric, mystical nonsense, Section VII was kept quite secret from rest of the Technocracy. It was also, ultimately, a failure. The avatar, Bae, returned at the Chronicle's end after the PC's found the staff of Po Banyan, and is ready to be part of a new mage's Awakening. They also discovered the last two hidden barrels of John Chapman's apple jack and cider, the results of which are still rippling through a second chronicle (I had two concurrent games with different players; the 2nd of those games is ongoing). You just can't keep a good avatar down.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12765-otto-d-fey","name":"Otto D'Fey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12765_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"44"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-30T12:06:00-07:00","id":1411109,"title":"","content":"Well, something had to happen with the Craftmasons, if they didn't become the basis of the NWO? And one could consider House Jannisary of the Order of Hermes to have been a secret Convention, after the Ksryifai (Pardon the spelling, it has been awhile since I've had to look that up) left. Realistically, there could be a Craft out there, working a secret Convention, more likely hiding out then there is one actively working for the Technocracy.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>THWarted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/17984-toby-weingarten","name":"Toby Weingarten","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"112"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-03T07:37:24-07:00","id":1411638,"title":"","content":"The Craftmasons didn't become the NWO, the Cabal of Pure Thought did. First they became the secular Lightkeepers then they got involved in a secret of British police detectives called the Skeleton Keys and became the NWO.<br /> <br /> We're not entirely sure what exactly happened with the Craftmasons with their destruction as some accounts contradicting each other, there seems to be two main lines of thought, either the Craftmasons were utterly wiped out or that some survived and were absorbed into the High Guild. Hell, the Technocracy Reloaded manuscript has only two mentions of them, one of which treats the historical existence of the Craftmasons with skepticism which isn't all that surprising as the Syndicate has taken credit for much of the Craftmasons' early successes and treating them more like a splinter of their progenitors that eventually went astray and they got rid of.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://youtu.be/_yBS2EZFduI?t=2m13s\" target=\"_blank\">Homo sapiens. What an inventive, invincible species. It's only a few million years since they crawled up out of the mud and learned to walk. Puny, defenceless bipeds. They've survived flood, famine and plague. They've survived cosmic wars and holocausts. And now, here they are, out among the stars, waiting to begin a new life. Ready to outsit eternity. They're indomitable. Indomitable.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/420-akatsukileader13","name":"AkatsukiLeader13","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar420_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1637"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-03T13:23:26-07:00","id":1411685,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AkatsukiLeader13</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1410842-what-about-secret-conventions-that-most-of-the-other-technocrats-don-t-know-exist?p=1411638#post1411638\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Craftmasons didn't become the NWO, the Cabal of Pure Thought did. First they became the secular Lightkeepers then they got involved in a secret of British police detectives called the Skeleton Keys and became the NWO.<br /> <br /> We're not entirely sure what exactly happened with the Craftmasons with their destruction as some accounts contradicting each other, there seems to be two main lines of thought, either the Craftmasons were utterly wiped out or that some survived and were absorbed into the High Guild. Hell, the Technocracy Reloaded manuscript has only two mentions of them, one of which treats the historical existence of the Craftmasons with skepticism which isn't all that surprising as the Syndicate has taken credit for much of the Craftmasons' early successes and treating them more like a splinter of their progenitors that eventually went astray and they got rid of.</div> </div> </div> </div>That is what Toby is saying, if they didn\u2019t become the NWO then they could have been the foundation of a secret convention, as they seem to already be scrubbed from history.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-03T13:43:13-07:00","id":1411686,"title":"","content":"In general, when a group in Mage gets \u201cwiped out\u201d but nonetheless manages to survive, it reappears shortly thereafter in some other guise. this is because in order to operate, you need to have some sort of front group. The most successful example of this are the Ksirafai, who disappeared from the Order of Reason only to have been revealed centuries later to have infiltrated the Order of Hermes as House Janissary. Other destroyed groups tended to re-emerge as Crafts, like the Children of Knowledge or the Templar, formerly Solificati and Cabal of Pure Thought, respectively. <br /> <br /> So if the Craftmasons survived, what's their front group?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-04T09:08:40-07:00","id":1411808,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1410842-what-about-secret-conventions-that-most-of-the-other-technocrats-don-t-know-exist?p=1411686#post1411686\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In general, when a group in Mage gets \u201cwiped out\u201d but nonetheless manages to survive, it reappears shortly thereafter in some other guise. this is because in order to operate, you need to have some sort of front group. The most successful example of this are the Ksirafai, who disappeared from the Order of Reason only to have been revealed centuries later to have infiltrated the Order of Hermes as House Janissary. Other destroyed groups tended to re-emerge as Crafts, like the Children of Knowledge or the Templar, formerly Solificati and Cabal of Pure Thought, respectively.<br /> <br /> So if the Craftmasons survived, what's their front group?</div> </div> </div> </div>The Sons of Ether?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2783-tytalus","name":"Tytalus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2783_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"491"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-04T15:19:47-07:00","id":1411904,"title":"","content":"What if the Craftmasons became something like the Continuum Corp of Engineers Quantum Architects, using sublime mathematics to form the base of the secret covenants?<br /> <br /> So we have the <br /> <br /> Quantum Architects- formerly Craftmasons, Prime Sphere.<br /> <br /> <br /> The Investigators of Temporal Harmony- formerly Kisarafai acts as secret continuum polices.<br /> <br /> The Cartographers of Continuum- Formerly Celestial Masters they map out new Timelines and the Multiverse and Beyond.<br /> <br /> And they are grooming the Void Engineers to join them, faking their eventual downfall.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-05T11:10:04-07:00","id":1412118,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AkatsukiLeader13</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1410842-what-about-secret-conventions-that-most-of-the-other-technocrats-don-t-know-exist?p=1411638#post1411638\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">We're not entirely sure what exactly happened with the Craftmasons with their destruction...</div> </div> </div> </div>The destruction of the Craftmasons is supposed to represent the Order of Reason, and the Technocracy betraying its moral and ethical roots and turning on the common people and laborers who created it and that the Conventions are supposed to represent and defend.<br /> <br /> Most of the Craftmasons were murdered, with some being absorbed into other groups.<br /> <br /> As for secret groups inside the Techno's, how about<br /> <br /> <i>The Doomsday Actuaries </i><br /> <br /> A trans-convention group, with members among the NWO, Syndicate, Iteration X and Void Engineer, they are always computing the likelyhood of failure and disaster to individual plans and the Technocracy as a larger entity. No one likes having them around because they are hella depressing but never offer better ideas except to go forwards. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1208,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1208-grumpy-rpg-reviews","user":"Grumpy RPG Reviews","date":". 09-05-2020, 02:19 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1208-grumpy-rpg-reviews","name":"Grumpy RPG Reviews","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1208_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1888"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}